[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62309,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Non-gestational choriocarcinoma is a malignant tumour composed of cytotrophoblast and syncytiotrophoblast that is not of gestational origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62310,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9100/3 Choriocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62311,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C73.Y &amp; XH8PK7 Other specified malignant neoplasms of the ovary &amp; Choriocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62312,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62313,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62314,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most arise in the ovary, but they rarely may involve the periadnexal or pelvic soft tissue {28877059; 31421690}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62315,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour affects children and young adults. Patients present with abdominal pain, pelvic mass, and vaginal bleeding or (rarely) haemoperitoneum. Serum &beta;-hCG is typically elevated. As many as half of premenarchal patients have isosexual precocious puberty. Rarely, ovarian epithelial cancers in older women may contain foci of choriocarcinoma, but such foci are probably of somatic tumour origin rather than germ cell origin {19809555; 25105109; 28877059; 31421690}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62316,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Non-gestational choriocarcinoma is very rare, with only a few reported cases and accounting for &lt;&nbsp;1% of all ovarian neoplasms {27073524}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62317,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62318,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In children and young women, these tumours are of germ cell origin. In rare cases occurring in older women with an ovarian epithelial cancer that contains foci of choriocarcinoma, the foci probably derive from the somatic tumour {28877059; 16527336; 31421690}. Short tandem repeat (STR) DNA genotyping of non-gestational choriocarcinoma reveals an allelic pattern identical to that of the patient&rsquo;s normal tissue. Allelic imbalances may also be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62319,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are typically large, solid, haemorrhagic, and necrotic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62320,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>The tumour consists of an admixture of mononuclear cytotrophoblast and multinucleated syncytiotrophoblast, often accompanied by extensive haemorrhage and necrosis, which may obscure the tumour cells. Some tumours are composed predominantly of mononuclear trophoblast. Tumour cells are positive by hCG immunohistochemistry. The tumour may be pure or may present as a component of a mixed germ cell tumour. In older women, foci of choriocarcinoma may be present within an ovarian epithelial carcinoma {16527336; 20707961; 20881859}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-09T15:21:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62321,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62322,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>STR DNA genotyping can be used to distinguish non-gestational choriocarcinoma from an ovarian metastasis of uterine or tubal gestational choriocarcinoma, which would be expected to contain non-maternal alleles of paternal origin {28877059; 31421690}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62323,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> biphasic tumour composed of mononuclear trophoblast and syncytiotrophoblast of non-gestational origin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62324,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>This entity is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:39:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62325,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 89,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Non-gestational choriocarcinoma has more-frequent lymphatic and intraperitoneal spread and may be less chemosensitive than gestational choriocarcinoma. Choriocarcinoma associated with ovarian epithelial carcinoma has a poor prognosis {29894083; 20881859; 28877059}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:53:07"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]